# Project Architecture (aetlier-admin)

Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, **JavaScript `.jsx`**, Redux Toolkit + RTK Query, Tailwind v4 + HeroUI v3. Yarn. Port 3001. See `AGENTS.md`.

```
app/                      Routes (PRIMARY — ignore legacy src/app/)
  login/ auth/callback/   Auth entry + SSO
  (dashboard)/            Route group — NOT in URL
components/layout/        AdminLayout, Sidebar, Header
components/ui/            Shared barrel exports
features/                 Domain modules
redux/services/api.js     Single createApi slice (all REST)
lib/validation/           Zod schemas
utils/permissions.js      Client permission helpers
```

## Hard rules
- Most pages are `'use client'`; root is `force-dynamic`.
- All REST endpoints live in `redux/services/api.js` with tag caching. Axios `apiClient` only for auth profile in `authSlice`.
- Portal entry: `canAccessAdminPortal` / `admin.portal.access`; roles may set portal redirect flags.
- Permission strings must stay aligned with backend `resource.action.scope`.
- Tailwind config is via `hero.ts` / `@config` in `globals.css` — not classic `tailwind.config.js`.
- HeroUI v3: import from `@/lib/heroui` (v2-compatible wrappers). Do not import `@heroui/react` in pages.
